# Citation File Format — https://citation-file-format.github.io
#
# GitHub reads this and shows a "Cite this repository" button on the repo page,
# offering APA and BibTeX. Zenodo and several reference managers read it too.
#
# NOTE ON THE NAME: CFF has no separate middle-name field. The spec puts ALL
# given names in `given-names`, so "Tim Casanda" is correct and renders as
# "Gibson, T. C." — the conventional form. Do not move Casanda to a particle
# field; `name-particle` is for things like "van" or "de".
#
# `version` and `date-released` should be bumped alongside APP_VERSION in
# global.R when a release is worth citing.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EasyAnalysis in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "EasyAnalysis: point-and-click statistical, machine-learning and spatial analysis"
abstract: >-
  EasyAnalysis is a free, local-first platform for running statistical,
  machine-learning and spatial/geospatial analysis without writing code. It
  installs on the user's own computer and runs there, so data being analysed
  never leaves the machine. It covers statistical modelling, machine learning,
  and spatial, raster, terrain, hydrology and LiDAR workflows, and includes an
  AI assistant that runs the application's own analyses and explains results.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Tim Casanda"
    family-names: Gibson
repository-code: "https://github.com/Casanda00/easyanalysis"
url: "https://easyanalysis.dev"
# GPL-3.0 is forced by the dependency graph, not chosen for taste: the app
# cannot run without GPL-3-only R packages (lidR, terra, MASS, nnet, ape,
# shinyWidgets, leaflet.extras, base64enc, ggspatial). See COPYRIGHT.
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.10.16
date-released: "2026-08-06"
# Add the Zenodo DOI here after the first archived release — see .zenodo.json.
# identifiers:
#   - type: doi
#     value: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
#     description: Concept DOI for all versions
keywords:
  - statistics
  - machine learning
  - spatial analysis
  - geospatial
  - remote sensing
  - LiDAR
  - GIS
  - R
  - Shiny
  - reproducible research
